Codex is being used to analyze a large OpenAPI specification (~68,000 lines) to identify the correct API endpoints required for test automation. Due to the absence of comprehensive documentation or SMEs, manual endpoint discovery is extremely time-consuming. Codex understands the API contracts and maps functional requirements to the appropriate endpoints, significantly improving productivity. The current token limit restricts analysis of such a large specification, so an increased token allocation is required to efficiently complete the project's automation scenarios.
